                        to support the attribution has been supplied from <title>Catalogue of very
                           important illuminated &amp; other manuscripts, the property of the Lord
                           Mostyn ... which will be sold by auction ... on Tuesday, the 13th of
                           July, 1920</title> (London, 1920), lot 38: 'In 1487 the MS. was in the
                        possession of <persName role="fmo">Richard Brynkley</persName>, who has
                        written his name, and the date in Greek letters, at the end. This Richard
                        Brynkley was an important official of the Franciscan Order in
                     England'.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Mostyn sale (Sotheby, 13 July 1920), lot 38
                     to Maggs, who sold to S. Babra of Barcelona in 1923. This was the last known
                     provenance according to the second edition of Medieval Libraries of Great
                     Britain (1964), p. 24. The book remains untraced.</provenance>
